---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/pages/privacy.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | LIT Bible"
  description="The LIT Bible website and app privacy policy. Your reading life is your own — we collect nothing personally identifiable, and everything you create stays on your device."
  canonical="https://litbible.net/privacy"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "Privacy Policy — LIT Bible",
      "url": "https://litbible.net/privacy",
      "dateModified": "2026-04-08",
      "description": "The LIT Bible website and app privacy policy. Your reading life is your own — we collect nothing personally identifiable, and everything you create stays on your device.",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@type": "WebSite",
        "name": "LIT Bible",
        "url": "https://litbible.net"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "LIT Bible",
        "url": "https://litbible.net"
      }
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="privacy-page" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">

    <header class="privacy-header">
      <div class="privacy-header__inner">
        <h1 id="privacy-title" class="privacy-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="privacy-effective">
          Effective date: <time datetime="2026-04-08">April 8, 2026</time>
        </p>
        <p class="privacy-lede">
          The LIT Bible is built on a simple principle: your reading life is
          your own. This policy describes what data the LIT Bible website
          (litbible.net) and iOS app collect and how.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-body">

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-scope">
        <h2 id="privacy-scope">Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This policy applies to both the LIT Bible website at litbible.net
          and the LIT Bible iOS app. Where a section applies only to one or
          the other, it is labeled accordingly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-collect">
        <h2 id="privacy-collect">What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Website:</strong> The only personal information we collect is
          your email address, and only if you choose to subscribe to our mailing
          list. We use Brevo to manage our mailing list. Your email address is
          stored with Brevo and used solely to send you LIT Bible updates. You
          can unsubscribe at any time using the link in any email we send.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand how the site is used.
          Cloudflare Web Analytics is privacy-preserving by design: it does not
          use cookies, does not track individuals across sites or sessions, and
          does not build behavioral profiles. The data it collects — such as
          page view counts and general geographic region — is aggregated and
          cannot be used to identify you. Cloudflare, our hosting provider, may
          also log basic request data (such as IP addresses) at the network
          level for security and performance purposes. All Cloudflare data
          handling is subject to{" "}
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>App:</strong> The app does not collect your name, email
          address, device identifiers, or any information that could identify
          you as an individual.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-on-device">
        <h2 id="privacy-on-device">What stays on your device (app)</h2>
        <p>
          Everything you create in the app — highlights, notes, and your reading
          position — is stored locally on your device using a private database.
          This data never leaves your device and is not accessible to us.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your app preferences (such as your chosen text size and whether you
          have completed the welcome tour) are stored in your device's standard
          preferences storage and remain on your device.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-content-updates">
        <h2 id="privacy-content-updates">Content updates (app)</h2>
        <p>
          The app may periodically check our servers at litbible.net for updates
          to the Bible translation text. During this check, your device contacts
          our server and downloads any changed content. No information about you,
          your device, or your reading activity is sent to us during this
          process. The check is limited to comparing file versions and
          downloading updated text — nothing more.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-spotlight">
        <h2 id="privacy-spotlight">Spotlight Search (app)</h2>
        <p>
          The app makes portions of the Bible text available through your
          device's built-in Spotlight search. This indexing happens entirely on
          your device and is not transmitted to us or to Apple.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-widget">
        <h2 id="privacy-widget">The home screen widget (app)</h2>
        <p>
          The LIT Bible widget displays lectionary readings and liturgical
          calendar information. All widget data is computed on your device from
          information bundled with the app. The widget makes no network
          requests.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-external-links">
        <h2 id="privacy-external-links">External links</h2>
        <p>
          The website and app include links to external services. When you
          follow these links, you are subject to those third parties' own
          privacy policies. We do not track whether you visit these pages or
          take any action on them.
        </p>
        <p>External services we link to include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Donorbox</strong> — for contributions to the LIT Bible and
            the Liberating Scripture Collective
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Apple Podcasts</strong> — for the Found in Translation
            podcast
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Spotify</strong> — for the Found in Translation podcast
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>YouTube</strong> — for the Found in Translation podcast
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>CreativeCommons.org</strong> — to display the full license
            text
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>liberatingscripture.org</strong> — the Liberating Scripture
            Collective's website
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-sharing">
        <h2 id="privacy-sharing">Sharing (app)</h2>
        <p>
          When you select text and choose Share, your device's standard share
          sheet opens. The selected passage text is passed to whatever app you
          choose to share it with. We do not log what you share, where you share
          it, or how often.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-third-party">
        <h2 id="privacy-third-party">Third-party software (app)</h2>
        <p>The app is built using two third-party software libraries:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>GRDB</strong> — an open-source database library. It stores
            your data locally on your device and makes no network connections of
            its own.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Supabase SDK</strong> — a library that supports optional
            cloud backup features. This feature is not active in the current
            version of the app. The library is included in preparation for a
            future update; it makes no network connections and does not collect
            any data in the current version.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-children">
        <h2 id="privacy-children">Children</h2>
        <p>
          The LIT Bible website and app do not collect personal information from
          anyone, including children. The site and app contain no advertising
          and no social features. The only personal data collected — email
          addresses for the newsletter — requires active opt-in and is never
          required to access any content.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-changes">
        <h2 id="privacy-changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we update this policy in a way that is material to how your data is
          handled, we will note it in the app's Translation Updates section and
          on the website, and update the effective date above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-contact">
        <h2 id="privacy-contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy can be directed to the LIT Bible team at
          <a href="/contact">litbible.net/contact</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
